# An instruction the classifier does not model inside a loop of param_1
# trips: per thread the kernel's cuda-core FLOPs are its f32 ones,
# 2·param_1, which are what was counted, and an unknown part; its
# tensor, sfu and atomic FLOPs and its shared bytes are unknown, and its
# global bytes lower bounds. The loop's instructions list the
# `wgmma.fence`, AI(global) has no direction because both sides are
# lower bounds, and the kernel's unknowns name the instruction.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/unknown_in_loop.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/unknown_in_loop.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_unknown_in_loop( // per thread: flops f32 2·param_1 + ?; tensor, sfu, atomic flops ?; global load >= 4·param_1 B, store >= 4·param_1 B; shared load ? B, store ? B; param load 12 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_2: // loop: trips param_1 | under line 29 | exec param_1/thread{{$}}
CHECK: wgmma.fence.sync.aligned  1
CHECK: AI(global): not bounded (flops are a lower bound, global bytes are a lower bound)
CHECK: unknowns:
CHECK: instruction `wgmma` x1 — not classified — its flops/bytes are not counted
